{
 "spec": "trial-readings/1",
 "reading": "one row per animation set, from scripts/measure.py over rigc render --geometry --folds --seam --pass-through. A seam pair is [gap, ghost], the worst frame of the set, in cells of one rig px. pass = pass-through frames summed over both pairs. folds = meshes with a folded triangle on any frame. feet.<side> = [ankle y min, ankle y max, ankle x min, ankle x max, lowest foot vertex y min, max], world units (rig px, y up). Hold-pose sets (suffix 000/025/050/075/100) were read at 4 fps; beats at 4 fps (split/unsplit) or 24 fps (cloth, settle).",
 "series": {
  "n": "unsplit rig (shoes one part, original l_ankle keypoint), two-bone IK, right ankle along the floor toward parallel to that rig's left leg (7.60 deg, 88.0 px at 100%)",
